er yard, convict stockade and a series of shipping and railway-related buildings.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Convict Lumber Yard","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/570_-_Convict_Lumber_Yard_or_Stockade_Site_-_Interpretation_of_previous_structures_in_the_Convict_Lumber_Yard_%285044978b4%29.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/570_-_Convict_Lumber_Yard_or_Stockade_Site_-_Interpretation_of_previous_structures_in_the_Convict_Lumber_Yard_%285044978b4%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Bill Nethery","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:570_-_Convict_Lumber_Yard_or_Stockade_Site_-_Interpretation_of_previous_structures_in_the_Convict_Lumber_Yard_(5044978b4).jpg"}},{"id":"newcastle_horbury_hunt_hall","areaId":"newcastle","name":"Horbury Hunt Hall","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":-32.9298,"lng":151.7802},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"newcastle_horbury_hunt_hall","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":108,"wikiPageviews":23,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["horburyhunthall","newcastle"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Horbury Hunt Hall is a heritage-listed church hall at 52a Church Street, The Hill, New South Wales, a suburb of Newcastle in Australia. It was designed by John Horbury Hunt and built in 1878. It is also known as Christ Church Anglican Cathedral Hall. The property is owned by the Anglican Diocese of Newcastle.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Horbury Hunt Hall","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/156_-_Anglican_Cathedral_Hall%2C_Christ_Church_-_PCO_Plan_Number_156_%285044969p1%29.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/156_-_Anglican_Cathedral_Hall%2C_Christ_Church_-_PCO_Plan_Number_156_%285044969p1%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":1915